The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
hw->pctrl = devm_pinctrl_register(&pdev->dev, &mtk_desc, hw);
```
```c
/* Setup groups descriptions per SoC types */
err = mtk_build_groups(hw);
```
```c
/* Setup functions descriptions per SoC types */
err = mtk_build_functions(hw);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the pinctrl is being enabled before all groups and functions are added. The call to `devm_pinctrl_register` initializes the pinctrl device, but if this is done before the groups and functions are set up, it leads to an incomplete configuration, preventing `pinctrl_claim_hogs` from functioning correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
err = devm_pinctrl_register_and_init(&pdev->dev, &mtk_desc, hw, &hw->pctrl);
```
```c
err = pinctrl_enable(hw->pctrl);
```
Reason:
The fix involves using `devm_pinctrl_register_and_init`, which ensures that the pinctrl is not enabled until after all groups and functions have been added. This change maintains the correct sequence of operations, allowing `pinctrl_claim_hogs` to work as intended. The explicit call to `pinctrl_enable` after setting up the groups and functions ensures that the pinctrl is fully configured before it is activated.

